	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Setup — grant the caller a membership in the administration (ADR-005)",
			"description": "PeriodCloseController::show/aiFlags/transition all open with requireAccessibleAdministration(), which refuses with a masked 404 'Period not found' unless AdministrationContextService::canAccess() finds a valid AdministrationMembership for the caller. Being a Nextcloud admin does not imply one. Without this fixture every Period Close assertion below measures the membership guard instead of the close lifecycle — all seven were failing on 404 for exactly that reason, while VAT_Filings, which seeds the identical membership, passed 22/22 against the same administration_id.\n\nVAT_Filings also REVOKES its membership in its own teardown, and collections run alphabetically (TenderNed, VAT_Filings, bookings, shillinq), so this collection cannot piggyback on it — it has to seed its own.",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "POST AdministrationMembership for {{admin_user}} on {{administration_id}}",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('membership created or already present', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 201]));",
									"const body = pm.response.json();",
									"const id = body.id || body['@self']?.id;",
									"if (id) { pm.collectionVariables.set('membership_id', id); }"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"url": "{{base_url}}/index.php/apps/openregister/api/objects/shillinq/AdministrationMembership",
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\"userId\":\"{{admin_user}}\",\"administrationId\":\"{{administration_id}}\",\"role\":\"eigenaar\",\"mayPostJournalEntries\":true,\"mayCloseFiscalYear\":true}"
						}
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "Period Close",
			"description": "bookkeeping-period-close (T2): guided close lifecycle + AI close-assistant flags.\n\nThe folder SEEDS ITS OWN FiscalPeriod fixtures (adm-smb-1: 2026-01 audit-locked, 2026-02 closed, 2026-04 open) and deletes them again at the end. It used to assume they were already present, but nothing in the product creates them: PeriodCloseBackfill seeds a rolling FORWARD horizon (current month + twelve), which by construction never contains a period in the past, and BackfillFiscalPeriods only materialises periods that historical GLLine rows already reference. On a fresh install `GET /apps/openregister/api/objects/shillinq/FiscalPeriod` returns zero rows, so all seven assertions below were asserting against 404 rather than against the close lifecycle. Seeding them here makes the folder self-contained and makes the assertions actually exercise the transitions.",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Setup — seed the 2026-04 open period",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"url": "{{base_url}}/index.php/apps/openregister/api/objects/shillinq/FiscalPeriod",
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"periodId\": \"{{period_id_open}}\",\n  \"name\": \"April 2026\",\n  \"administrationId\": \"{{administration_id}}\",\n  \"startDate\": \"2026-04-01\",\n  \"endDate\": \"2026-04-30\",\n  \"fiscalYear\": 2026,\n  \"state\": \"open\",\n  \"reopenedHistory\": [],\n  \"taskChecklistItems\": [],\n  \"aiFlags\": []\n}"
						},
						"description": "Fixture for the open → closing → closed path."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('open period fixture created', function () {",
									"    pm.expect([200, 201]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
									"    const body = pm.response.json();",
									"    const uuid = body.id || body['@self']?.id || body.uuid;",
									"    pm.expect(uuid).to.be.a('string').and.not.equal('');",
									"    pm.collectionVariables.set('fixture_period_open_uuid', String(uuid));",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Setup — seed the 2026-02 closed period",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"url": "{{base_url}}/index.php/apps/openregister/api/objects/shillinq/FiscalPeriod",
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"periodId\": \"{{period_id_closed}}\",\n  \"name\": \"February 2026\",\n  \"administrationId\": \"{{administration_id}}\",\n  \"startDate\": \"2026-02-01\",\n  \"endDate\": \"2026-02-28\",\n  \"fiscalYear\": 2026,\n  \"state\": \"closed\",\n  \"closedAt\": \"2026-03-05T10:00:00+00:00\",\n  \"closedBy\": \"admin\",\n  \"reopenedHistory\": [],\n  \"taskChecklistItems\": [],\n  \"aiFlags\": []\n}"
						},
						"description": "Fixture for the reopen path (REQ-PC-006)."
					},
					"event": [
						{
